    "summary": "Cross-user cache disclosure and poisoning in Next.js use cache with binary arguments",
    "description": "<!-- https://linear.app/vercel/issue/NSEC-546 -->\r\nNext.js App Router applications that pass binary arguments (such as Uint8Array or Blob values) to functions using the `use cache` directive can produce identical cache keys for distinct arguments, allowing cached results to be shared across users \u2014 cross-user disclosure of cached data or cache poisoning. This affects applications using `use cache` with binary arguments.",
